@startuml
!include theme.iuml
title Preserved desktop row and selected-editor lifecycle
state "Unsaved draft" as Draft
state "Check new entry" as CheckNew <<choice>>
state "Stored entry\n(not necessarily approved)" as Persisted
state "Selected editor\nmay contain unsaved changes" as Selected
state "Check edit" as CheckEdit <<choice>>
state "Await confirmation" as Confirm
state "Deletion attempt" as DeleteAttempt
state "Creation attempt" as CreateAttempt
state "Edit attempt" as EditAttempt
state "Deleted row" as Deleted
[*] --> Draft
Draft --> Draft : attachment staged / invalidate review
Draft --> CheckNew : Save
CheckNew --> Draft : [blank or audio unfinished] / show warning
CheckNew --> CreateAttempt : [valid and audio ready]
CreateAttempt --> Draft : write failed / retain draft
CreateAttempt --> Persisted : committed / reset Collect form
Persisted --> Selected : select cached row / populate editor
Selected --> Selected : evidence edited / invalidate approval
Selected --> CheckEdit : Save changes
CheckEdit --> Selected : [blank] / retain edits
CheckEdit --> EditAttempt : [valid]
EditAttempt --> Selected : committed / refresh without changing identity
EditAttempt --> Selected : stale ID or write failed / retain edits + error
Selected --> Confirm : Delete
Confirm --> Selected : No / no mutation
Confirm --> DeleteAttempt : Yes
DeleteAttempt --> Selected : stale ID or write failed / retain edits + error
DeleteAttempt --> Deleted : committed / clear selection
Deleted --> [*]
legend bottom
  Desktop compatibility view; web account/project lifecycle is separate.
  This is a logical row/editor model, not an implemented enum or whole-app lifecycle.
  The selected editor may outlive a row removed by another writer; stale errors are explicit.
  A successful commit is not reversed by later display/cleanup failure.
  Audio staging has a separate lifetime; deleting a saved row retains its recording.
endlegend
@enduml
